Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight Private Permit Bridge P0 Solution

@ [solution_uuid] cb8e5676-87c5-4fe1-a2b4-5a08cc6dc5c5
@ [canonical_uuid] 06d82d16-143a-4abb-9c70-c03163285842
@ [design_uuid] 2dc1c5cb-cb35-4e88-bf36-a0d31460c84e

& [Waist]
  + one opaque admission owned by one private bridge core
  + one consuming runner issuer creates the existing opaque permit
  + one immediate FnOnce move enters the existing runner
  + one canonical reparse and existing validator convert returned run truth into one terminal non-capability outcome

& [VisibilitySolution]
  + crate-private module declaration and items with private fields no public re-export and no binary or ambient dispatcher
  + reserve a later nested live_initiation child as the only eligible production constructor locus; current implementation has none
  + child unit tests use direct private literals rather than a constructor symbol

& [TransitionTable]
  + candidate plus invalid pure input yields refused_before_issuance permits0 runner invocations0
  + validated candidate plus move into issuer yields permit_issued admission0 permit1
  + permit_issued plus immediate FnOnce call yields attempt_spent permit0 runner invocations1
  + attempt_spent plus runner error yields terminal abandoned_after_consumption
  + attempt_spent plus canonical receipt replay refusal yields terminal receipt_refused
  + attempt_spent plus verified unavailable run yields terminal completed_provider_unavailable
  + attempt_spent plus verified available run yields terminal completed_available
  + every terminal has admission0 permit0 retry0 and no outgoing edge

& [VerifierSolution]
  + formation verifier binds exact immutable SJS artifacts and counts without importing implementation
  + later implementation independently reuses activation validation producer-plan verification runner canonical serialization parsing and validation rather than trusting the bridge return
  + static gates examine module declaration item visibility derives constructor count runner call count absence patterns and binary inventory

& [FailureSolution]
  + perform all pure checks before issuance
  + regard issuance as the point of irreversible attempt authority expenditure
  + convert all later failures to data-only terminal outcomes so Rust ownership and result types cannot reconstitute capability

& [Boundary]
  + formation is meaning only and implementation remains structurally unreachable; live initiation and every physical effect require a later independently signed contract
